# Studio Queral Responsive Text System

## CORE RESPONSIVE TEXT PRINCIPLES

### 1. MOBILE-FIRST RESPONSIVE FONT SCALE
Always start with mobile-optimized sizes, then scale up:

**Primary Text Hierarchy:**
- `f7 f6-ns f5-l` - Small text (captions, dates, meta)
- `f6 f5-ns f4-l` - Body text (paragraphs, standard content)  
- `f5 f4-ns f3-l` - Large body text (emphasis, lead paragraphs)
- `f4 f3-ns f2-l` - Small headings (h4, h5)
- `f3 f2-ns f1-l` - Medium headings (h3)
- `f2 f1-ns f-subheadline-l` - Large headings (h2)
- `f1 f-subheadline-ns f-headline-l` - Hero headings (h1)

### 2. LINE HEIGHT STANDARDS
- `lh-copy` (1.5) - Default for body text
- `lh-title` (1.25) - For headings and short text blocks
- `lh-solid` (1.0) - For display text and logos only

### 3. READING MEASURE (LINE LENGTH)
- `measure` (30em) - Optimal for body text
- `measure-wide` (34em) - For larger text or special content
- `measure-narrow` (20em) - For sidebar content or captions

### 4. RESPONSIVE SPACING PATTERNS
**Margins:**
- `mb2 mb3-ns` - Small spacing between elements
- `mb3 mb4-ns` - Standard spacing between sections
- `mb4 mb5-ns` - Large spacing between major sections

**Padding:**
- `pa3 pa4-ns` - Container/card padding
- `ph3 ph4-ns pv3 pv4-ns` - Specific control over horizontal/vertical

### 5. FONT WEIGHT HIERARCHY
- `normal` - Body text (400)
- `fw6` - Emphasis within body text (600)  
- `b` - Strong emphasis and small headings (700)
- `fw3` - Light text for de-emphasis (300)

## IMPLEMENTATION RULES

### Standard Body Text Pattern:
```html
<p class="f6 f5-ns lh-copy measure">Your content here</p>
```

### Article/Post Content Pattern:
```html
<div class="f6 f5-ns lh-copy measure-wide">
  <h2 class="f3 f2-ns lh-title mb3 mb4-ns">Heading</h2>
  <p class="mb3 mb4-ns">Paragraph content...</p>
</div>
```

### Card/Component Content Pattern:
```html
<div class="pa3 pa4-ns">
  <h3 class="f4 f3-ns lh-title mb2 mb3-ns">Card Title</h3>
  <p class="f6 f5-ns lh-copy">Card content...</p>
</div>
```

### Navigation/UI Text Pattern:
```html
<a class="f6 f5-ns ph2 ph3-ns pv1 pv2-ns">Link Text</a>
```

## BREAKPOINT REFERENCE
- No suffix = Default (mobile)
- `-ns` = Not small (30em+, ~480px+)
- `-m` = Medium (30em-60em, ~480px-960px)  
- `-l` = Large (60em+, ~960px+)

## ACCESSIBILITY REQUIREMENTS
- Minimum font size: f7 (0.75rem, ~12px)
- Minimum line height: 1.4 for body text
- Maximum line length: 75 characters (~measure-wide)
- Ensure sufficient color contrast (4.5:1 minimum)

## MOBILE-SPECIFIC CONSIDERATIONS
- Increase touch targets: minimum 44px height for interactive elements
- Use larger spacing on mobile: prefer `mb3` over `mb2` on small screens  
- Consider thumb-friendly navigation zones
- Test with iOS Dynamic Type and Android font scaling

## COMMON PATTERNS TO AVOID
- Fixed px font sizes in CSS
- Single breakpoint responsive (use mobile-first progression)
- Overly long lines on desktop (always use measure classes)
- Inconsistent spacing (stick to the scale)

## TEMPLATE CONSISTENCY CHECKLIST
- [ ] All body text uses f6 f5-ns minimum
- [ ] All text blocks use lh-copy or lh-title  
- [ ] All content containers use measure/measure-wide
- [ ] All spacing follows mb2/mb3/mb4 + -ns pattern
- [ ] All interactive elements have proper touch targets
- [ ] Navigation uses responsive padding (ph2 ph3-ns pv1 pv2-ns) 